# Line endings for the vendored racoons tree (ticket 161).
#
# The vendored sources are upstream blobs copied byte for byte, and upstream
# stores them with LF endings. Without an attribute, `core.autocrlf=true` makes
# this checkout write CRLF into the working tree while the index keeps LF, so
# every vendored file shows a `git status` modification that has no content
# change. A re-sync that writes the honest LF bytes then turns that into 146
# phantom entries that cannot be told apart from the 31 real ones.
#
# Pin the vendored paths to LF so checkout and re-sync agree with the blobs and
# `git status` stays readable. Do not convert this tree to CRLF: byte equality
# with the pin is the promise recorded in vendor/racoons/PROVENANCE.md.
vendor/racoons/** text eol=lf
